  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Through FY2026 to date, the Department of Commerce obligated $3.3B on federal contracts across 6,393 awards, with an average award size of $518K. Obligations fell 20.3% year over year. Fiscal year totals show variation: FY21 was $4.5B, FY22 was $4.1B, FY23 was $5B, FY24 was $5.2B, FY25 was $4.2B, and FY26 is $3.3B. The largest categories so far this fiscal year are technology and services oriented, led by Other Computer Related Services at $604M, Computer Systems Design Services at $499M, and Custom Computer Programming Services at $339M. Commerce also obligated $220M to All Other Publishers and $147M each to Ship Building and Repairing and Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services. The top vendors by obligations in FY2026 to date include REED TECHNOLOGY AND INFORMATION SERVICES LLC at $218M, ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC at $110M, and LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $108M. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Commerce's contract spending changed over recent years?",
        "body": "Obligations peaked at $5.2B in FY24 and are $3.3B in FY26 to date. Year over year, obligations fell 20.3%. Annual totals were $4.5B in FY21, $4.1B in FY22, $5B in FY23, and $4.2B in FY25. These figures are contract obligations, with FY26 shown as a fiscal year to date total."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where is Commerce spending in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Technology and professional services dominate spending, with Other Computer Related Services at $604M, Computer Systems Design Services at $499M, and Custom Computer Programming Services at $339M. Commerce also obligated $220M to All Other Publishers and $147M each to Ship Building and Repairing and Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services. The top vendors include REED TECHNOLOGY AND INFORMATION SERVICES LLC at $218M, ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC at $110M, and LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $108M."
      }
    ]
